; ── Euro Connector Plug (SNSP-015): SCART to three phono jacks ───────────────────
;
; A rigid black block, no cord: its SCART shell goes straight into a set's SCART IN,
; and a console's composite lead goes into its three jacks. ScartAdapter is an
; AvAdapter of ONE plug, PlugA0, which IS the block: no PlugB0 and no VerletRope.
;
; ── The frame ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; PlugA0's frame is RetroXR's plug frame: the origin on the collar's face, where a
; SCART socket's shroud stops it; the shell along +Z into the socket, the block and
; the jacks behind it along -Z, the lettering +Y. The model is exported in its own
; frame (shell -Y, lettering +Z), so Shell is turned a quarter about X: a model point
; (x, y, z) is (x, z, -y) here. Its jacks' mouths, the model's RcaJackVideo (+15 mm X),
; RcaJackL (0) and RcaJackR (-15 mm X), are 43.0 mm back and 2.0 mm down.
;
; Each jack's zone is its MOUTH, turned R_x(180) so the mouth faces PlugA0 -Z (as on
; TrsRcaAdapter). IN, signal_kind 0 (TvSignal.Kind.COMPOSITE): the jacks are the set's
; SCART input's (AdapterRcaPort). show_jack is off: the model draws them.
[node name="ScartAdapter" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_script")
cord_colors = PackedColorArray(0.086, 0.086, 0.094, 1)

